{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban","id":1039383,"title":"ban","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-28T05:41:28-08:00","id":1039383,"title":"ban","content":"Given the barrier that a normal ban errects prevents all phenomena from crossing its border, what happens when the spell is cast as an aoe where the borders go through objects/creatures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:48:17-08:00","id":1039386,"title":"","content":"I'd say that it locks them in place.<br /> Edit: Or add Reach option to push them either way with some bashing damage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T06:26:58-08:00","id":1039397,"title":"","content":"We've always played that bisecting someone with a Ban kills them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T06:36:38-08:00","id":1039399,"title":"","content":"At my table Ban is more 'soft?' in touch but Inodivs interpretation is totally fine. It should probably be withstood in this case, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T08:38:49-08:00","id":1039429,"title":"","content":"A Ban exists to say &quot;The path between A and B doesn't exist for X&quot;. If a target is transitioning between A and B, it's shunted <i>out</i> of that path and carries on beyond it, just like every other target for a Ban would.<br /> <br /> Remember, a Ban isn't a forcefield; it's a space which that target can't pass through because that axis of space curves around the warded area. If I have a Ban against, say, rocks in the middle of an open room, if I throw a rock at it, the rock seems to pass through the Ban as if it were a portal. The same happens to a target half into the area; the spatial axis they're moving along bends and they bend with it. If they're inside the field already, they're not on that axis, so they're untouched.<br /> <br /> If there's a wall on the other side of the Ban, it'd be like the target collided at very high speed with that wall and would see them repelled. I'd treat it as I would them, say, running into a wall.<br /> <br /> Plus, you don't really want to give Space Mages the capacity to slice anything and everything in half at Space 3, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:31:21-08:00","id":1039459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039429#post1039429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, you don't really want to give Space Mages the capacity to slice anything and everything in half at Space 3, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Mind can easily instant-kill people at 2 dots with published spells.<br /> Matter + Forces + Death + Time can do it at 3 dots, again with published spells (although Death requires 2 spells to do it).<br /> With straightforward creative spells, Life joins the 'Two Dot Instagib' Club.<br /> (For a given value of Instant, eg turning an enemy into a baby at Time 3 is a death sentence if the mage wants it to be)<br /> <br /> If the path between A &amp; B doesn't exist, and half your body is where A is while the other half is where B is, it is very reasonable to rule that <i>you're fucked</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  Matter is in the three dot club, not the two dot club. My bad. 01-28-2017, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:59:33-08:00","id":1039469,"title":"","content":"The biggest weakness of Ban is that while it can be instant cast it can only be added to an existing Ward, which takes time to construct, so the real question is how strong do you want your characters to be in their own sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:02:56-08:00","id":1039471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039469#post1039469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest weakness of Ban is that while it can be instant cast it can only be added to an existing Ward</div> </div> </div> </div>Source? That might have been a 1E thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:03:49-08:00","id":1039472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039459#post1039459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> Mind + Matter can easily instant-kill people at 2 dots with published spells.<br /> Forces + Death + Time can do it at 3 dots, again with published spells (although Death requires 2 spells to do it).<br /> With straightforward creative spells, Life joins the 'Two Dot Instagib' Club.<br /> (For a given value of Instant, eg turning an enemy into a baby at Time 3 is a death sentence if the mage wants it to be)<br /> <br /> If the path between A &amp; B doesn't exist, and half your body is where A is while the other half is where B is, it is very reasonable to rule that <i>you're fucked</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No three dots spells easily kill people. Two dots even more so. I feel like you are missing some important facts about those spells. Tell me which spells out believe pull this off and how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:05:20-08:00","id":1039474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039472#post1039472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No three dots spells easily kill people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind \u2022\u2022 Psychic Domination. &quot;Kill yourself.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:07:39-08:00","id":1039475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039474#post1039474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind \u2022\u2022 Psychic Domination. &quot;Kill yourself.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So you not only invoke paradox in order to make the spell work at this level, but then you didn't read the text right and realize you only get to say one word commands. Cogratulations just you gave your enemy the order to &quot;kill.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:10:11-08:00","id":1039477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039475#post1039475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you not only invoke paradox in order to make the spell work at this level, but then you didn't read the text right and realize you only get to say one word commands. Cogratulations just you gave your enemy the order to &quot;kill.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but that is totally incorrect. The 2 Reach effect allows you to force a task, you're not limited to verbal commands.<br /> It literally says you can use it to make people kill themselves.<br /> If you have it as a rote, there's no Paradox risk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The task can be as complex or simple as the mage desires, giving the subject detailed mental instructions on how to go about completing the task. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage must spend one Mana when casting the spell.<br /> As with +1 Reach above, but the mage can force her subject to take any<br /> kind of action without limitations. For example, <b>the mage could direct<br /> her victim to shoot himself in the head</b>, or to run into a burning building. </div> </div> </div>Please familiarize yourself with the system before spreading misinformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-28-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:16:15-08:00","id":1039479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039477#post1039477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but that is totally incorrect. The 2 Reach effect allows you to force a task, you're not limited to verbal commands.<br /> It literally says you can use it to make people kill themselves.<br /> If you have it as a rote, there's no Paradox risk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Please familiarize yourself with the system before spreading misinformation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which you still need to do with one word commands. Reach for this spell to be effective. Instant cast, sensory range, 2 for deadly commands. Only a Master is not invoking paradox with this spell. Then we need spell factors. Ensure Potency and scale are right or else your spell fails entirely.<br /> <br /> Then at this point, you say &quot;Kill yourself&quot; You did not direct him to shoot himself in his head with one word commands, so at this point you once again have just given your enemy the order to &quot;Kill&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it possible? Sure you can direct your enemy to severely damage themselves. Is it practical or easy? No.<br /> <br /> Edit: I didn't even get into duration yet, which is also important for this spell to be effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","user":"Heroofthemists","date":". 01-28-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:20:21-08:00","id":1039482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039479#post1039479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which you still need to do with one word commands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... What? There's... There's a literal quote from the LITERAL RULE BOOK. Talking about how your commands are not limited to one word.<br /> Why ar eyou taking bits and pieces of things to make your point? It just makes you look ignorant of the system you're talking about, which... isn't a good look.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:21:21-08:00","id":1039484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039479#post1039479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which you still need to do with one word commands.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you do not need to do one word commands. Read the Reach effects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The task can be as complex or simple as the mage desires, giving the subject detailed mental instructions on how to go about completing the task.</span><br /> </i></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>My response was an off-the-cuff remark to your blatantly absurd assertion that you can't easily kill people with 3 dot or 2 dot spells. It was not meant to be a literal representation of the spell you'd cast to accomplish the effect. Yes, like all spells, you'd need Potency (you get two for free, and need 3 on average to affect someone, 6 to affect the strongest willed human being in existence) You are pointing to the basic building blocks of <i>all</i> spells (spell factors, reach effects, paradox risk) as if they are special limiters on the ability to kill people with magic.<br /> <br /> That's like saying killing someone with Disciplines is hard because you still have to spend vitae and roll dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only a Master is not invoking paradox with this spell. </div> </div> </div>Do you understand how rotes work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:22:49-08:00","id":1039485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039479#post1039479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: I didn't even get into duration yet, which is also important for this spell to be effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... not, really, though. If you're commanding someone to SHOOT THEMSELVES IN THE HEAD, they're... they're dead. That's one turn of action. That's all the duration you need. Because a dead person is not going to suddenly pop back up. NO ST I know will say, &quot;no loljk he's not still dead because your Duration wasn't long enough to... keep him dead? After he... died?<br /> <br /> ...what?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:25:55-08:00","id":1039487,"title":"","content":"&quot;Reach effect: The mage must spend one Mana when casting the spell.<br /> As with +1 Reach above, but the mage can force her subject to take any<br /> kind of action without limitations. For example, the mage could direct<br /> her victim to shoot himself in the head, or to run into a burning building&quot;<br /> <br /> It only allows your commands to have no limitations on their actions, as it had done until this point. At no point does it remove the fact you still need to give one word commands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:27:03-08:00","id":1039491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tenebra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039485#post1039485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's... not, really, though. If you're commanding someone to SHOOT THEMSELVES IN THE HEAD, they're... they're dead. That's one turn of action. That's all the duration you need. Because a dead person is not going to suddenly pop back up. NO ST I know will say, &quot;no loljk he's not still dead because your Duration wasn't long enough to... keep him dead? After he... died?<br /> <br /> ...what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh and that would be equally effective given any situation? A normal mortal sure. But any supernatural has a decent chance of surviving this shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:27:38-08:00","id":1039493,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#674EA7\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Psychic Domination</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Instant</b> - 2 Turns</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Rote (+3), High Speech (+2)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4 Free Reach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Instant, Sensory, Any Task</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>1 Overreach</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Advanced Duration</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Spell Factor</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency +2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Additional Spell Factors</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Potency +2 (-4), Duration +1 (-2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell sends a command telepathically to a subject in sensory range, providing </span></span><b><i>detailed mental instructions</i> for task that <i>can be as complex or simple as the mage desires, </i></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">forcing the subject to comply, even against their will. The subject will follow through even on clearly suicidal commands. This compulsion lasts for a day.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - 4 (Gnosis 2, Mind 3, Yantras 5, Spell Factors -6)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Paradox</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - 1 (1 Reach)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Releasing / Containing / Controlling</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Containing<br /> <br /> This is an actual spell used in one of my games. The Mage is Gnosis 2, Mind 3, has the spell as a Rote, and has 2 dots in the rote skill (it's an order rote skill). This is <i>not</i> a mage that was particularly specialized for this task.<br /> <br /> With Willpower, she has a Dicepool of 7. And Paradox? 33% of the time she might take 1 point of bashing from doing this. Otherwise, no meaningful Paradox.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-28-2017, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:28:20-08:00","id":1039494,"title":"","content":"&quot;+1 Reach: The mage is capable of taking control of her subject,<br /> forcing him to take actions against his will. The mage can force<br /> the subject to perform one task. <b>The task can be as complex or<br /> simple as the mage desires</b>, giving the subject detailed mental<br /> instructions on how to go about completing the task. She cannot<br /> force the subject to act in a way that would put him in serious<br /> danger, or to commit suicidal acts.&quot;<br /> <br /> THAT is the part you are ignoring.<br /> Please be thorough in your reading of the spell.<br /> The +2 Reach does not IGNORE the above Reach effect. It adds to it.<br /> As in, &quot;You may give your subject a COMPLEX command which he must follow by shooting himself in the head.&quot;<br /> That's what &quot;As with +1 Reach above&quot; means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:29:38-08:00","id":1039495,"title":"","content":"No, clearly when it says you can give the subject <b><i>detailed mental instructions</i> for task that <i>can be as complex or simple as the mage desires </i></b>you're still bound to make those instructions one word long.<br /> <br /> Clearly. I'm not being sarcastic at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039491#post1039491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh and that would be equally effective given any situation? A normal mortal sure. <b>But any supernatural has a decent chance of surviving this shot.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Shifting goal posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:32:55-08:00","id":1039497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039487#post1039487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Reach effect: The mage must spend one Mana when casting the spell.<br /> As with +1 Reach above, but the mage can force her subject to take any<br /> kind of action without limitations. For example, the mage could direct<br /> her victim to shoot himself in the head, or to run into a burning building&quot;<br /> <br /> It only allows your commands to have no limitations on their actions, as it had done until this point. At no point does it remove the fact you still need to give one word commands.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm also sincerely, genuinely curious how you can point this out, but ignore that the rule book itself clearly states you can &quot;direct her victim to <b>shoot himself in the head</b>&quot;, and interpret that as having to be done in a one word command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:34:20-08:00","id":1039498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039495#post1039495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, clearly when it says you can give the subject <b><i>detailed mental instructions</i> for task that <i>can be as complex or simple as the mage desires </i></b>you're still bound to make those instructions one word long.<br /> <br /> Clearly. I'm not being sarcastic at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shifting goal posts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not at all. I still maintain this is not easily done and requires one word commands. Granted these one word commands can be strung together if you are clever, but none the less one word commands. My point was in direct response to hers, not yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:36:57-08:00","id":1039499,"title":"","content":"Okay. Then maybe you'll understand this one.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Thetaskcanbeascomplexorsimpleasthemagedesires.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> I understand you maintain your own beliefs and that the rule book clearly details the ways in which you are wrong, but at least ACKNOWLEDGE the fact that the Reach effect ALLOWS SOMEONE to GIVE COMPLEX (as in NOT ONE WORD) commands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:37:05-08:00","id":1039500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039498#post1039498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. I still maintain this is not easily done and requires one word commands. Granted these one word commands can be strung together if you are clever, but none the less one word commands. My point was in direct response to hers, not yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, the example in the book is literally telling someone to shoot themselves in the head.<br /> The spell I demonstrated above shows a Disciple pulling this off with 4-7 dice (vs a target with up to 4 Withstand) and only a 33% chance of taking bashing damage from Paradox.<br /> <br /> Pick a different hill to die on and stop derailing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:39:53-08:00","id":1039502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039459#post1039459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the path between A &amp; B doesn't exist, and half your body is where A is while the other half is where B is, it is very reasonable to rule that <i>you're fucked</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about this is, it's not how the spell works. It's a <i>Weaving</i> spell, which reshapes the connections of local space. The path between A and B may not exist for the target but that doesn't manifest as a cut; it manifests as a redirection. The path from A to B now redirects to C, causing anything that is along that pathway to redirect. That's how the spell is described as working. It doesn't even target the ostensible victim's Pattern; just a zero-dimensional section of space around the caster and the sympathy between it and another region.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you want, you could technically apply this as it would logically work and note that this would separate the very atoms themselves that make up the target and the energetic release would cause a nuclear explosion that would evaporate everything in an enormous radius, but I just don't think that's the intended use of the Space arcanum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:40:07-08:00","id":1039503,"title":"","content":"The Example is &quot;direct someone to shoot themselves in the head&quot;. This suggest to me you need to wither string commands together, or be creative. Yes you can do it, but you can still only use one word commands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:41:40-08:00","id":1039504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039502#post1039502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about this is, it's not how the spell works. It's a <i>Weaving</i> spell, which reshapes the connections of local space. The path between A and B may not exist for the target but that doesn't manifest as a cut; it manifests as a redirection. The path from A to B now redirects to C, causing anything that is along that pathway to redirect. That's how the spell is described as working. It doesn't even target the ostensible victim's Pattern; just a zero-dimensional section of space around the caster and the sympathy between it and another region.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you want, you could technically apply this as it would logically work and note that this would separate the very atoms themselves that make up the target and the energetic release would cause a nuclear explosion that would evaporate everything in an enormous radius, but I just don't think that's the intended use of the Space arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it comes down to table preference honestly.<br /> My disagreement was more with the position that killing someone at 3 dots was out-of-theme than your interpretation of the spell, which is very appropriate and thematic for Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:43:26-08:00","id":1039505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039504#post1039504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it comes down to table preference honestly.<br /> My disagreement was more with the position that killing someone at 3 dots was out-of-theme than your interpretation of the spell, which is very appropriate and thematic for Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can respect that. Slicing someone in half with the Space Arcanum by saying &quot;This and this are no longer connected&quot; <i>is</i> very Space Arcanum, but that's more of a targeted Unraveling spell to my mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:44:56-08:00","id":1039506,"title":"","content":"While I'm kind of find with Space Mages having the ability to slice things in half, it sort of makes the same level spell warp and the higher level spell collapse to be kind of useless if you are saying that Ban is what is permitting that. Mind's ability to tell a person to kill themselves doesn't actually kill a person - it creates a set of circumstances in which a person is likely to die. It makes that person kill themselves - which, while likely, is not also a sure death either. You change a person's lungs to gills, or teleport them into a blazing fire - neither of these spells is directly the cause of the death of your target.<br /> <br /> If your spell is directly causing damage to an entity, rather than indirectly creating circumstances in which a person might die as a result, it may be best to consult the damage guides - bashing at 3 dots, lethal at 4, agg at 4 with manage, and autokill at 5. In this case, the spell isn't designed to damage or inflict - its creating a space in which certain things cannot enter or leave. It is not removing the space between those two things or anything and someone who is between the barrier is neither entering nor leaving - and when they move, they are either entering <b>or</b> leaving, not both - so one might decide the spells effects upon them based upon the direction they end up going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:45:58-08:00","id":1039507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039506#post1039506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it creates a set of circumstances in which a person is likely to die</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you could argue that trapping half of someone's body in a pocket dimension is the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:48:24-08:00","id":1039508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039507#post1039507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you could argue that trapping half of someone's body in a pocket dimension is the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it can. Trapping someone in Ban entirely makes more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:48:33-08:00","id":1039509,"title":"","content":"It's not Domination Discipline. You are not spending instant actions on a Mesmerized target to give them word-restricted commands. You are giving them detailed mental instructions on what to do. Killing people in this game is easy. Really really easy. To the point where plots that can be derailed or solved by killing stuff are about as hard as plots about punching goblin kindergarteners in DND.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:50:45-08:00","id":1039510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039509#post1039509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not Domination Discipline. You are not spending instant actions on a Mesmerized target to give them word-restricted commands. You are giving them detailed mental instructions on what to do. Killing people in this game is easy. Really really easy. To the point where plots that can be derailed or solved by killing stuff are about as hard as plots about punching goblin kindergarteners in DND.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair I think it can be ruled nearly the same. Anything longer than one word is not reflexive in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:58:52-08:00","id":1039514,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8177\" data-vbnamecard=\"8177\">Heroofthemists</a> While the rule does actually say 1 word commands initially, the first reach action is to remove that limitation. The 2 reach option removes that limitation and the safety limitation. Since it's mentally transmitted, a command longer than a word would be reflexive and the spell itself would be instant. You don't actually have to speak the words. Hell, at that point I wouldn't even say you had to transmit a sentence so much as an intent - you want them to kill themselves. *inserts image of them killing themselves*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039507#post1039507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you could argue that trapping half of someone's body in a pocket dimension is the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I'd say that could work. I mean, sounds like you'd be targeting a person and making the size of the spell less than the size of the target - which, as far as I'm aware, would not work. Could you perhaps show me, mechanically, how you might accomplish that example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:05:50-08:00","id":1039516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039507#post1039507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you could argue that trapping half of someone's body in a pocket dimension is the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity, I know at that level you can automatically kill a person. Thing is, the spell isn't designed to tear a person in half. It's designed to make a pocket dimension. If your cutting a person in half, you'd have better results unmaking the space that connects them together as a person than weaving the space of that piece of them. Your head is connected to your neck - unmake that connection and they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:20:23-08:00","id":1039521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039516#post1039516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For clarity, I know at that level you can automatically kill a person. Thing is, the spell isn't designed to tear a person in half. It's designed to make a pocket dimension. If your cutting a person in half, you'd have better results unmaking the space that connects them together as a person than weaving the space of that piece of them. Your head is connected to your neck - unmake that connection and they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ban <i>does</i> have a sidebar about how to use it to kill people. That said, it's not talking about bisecting, so like I mentioned to Axel before, I can totally understand not allowing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039510#post1039510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair I think it can be ruled nearly the same. Anything longer than one word is not reflexive in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nice. No one's talking about reflexive actions. <br /> The reach effects of the spell explicitly allows you to send detailed mental instructions for a task that can be as complex as you desire as part of the casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:46:10-08:00","id":1039679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039521#post1039521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's nice. No one's talking about reflexive actions.<br /> The reach effects of the spell explicitly allows you to send detailed mental instructions for a task that can be as complex as you desire as part of the casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they were talking about a relationship between dominate and mind, and explaining the mind doesn't have the limitation of Dominate. You have been very condescending when speaking to me, did you realize that? <br /> <br /> I disagree as the action being part of the casting. You are casting a spell to dominate their mind to allow you to send instructions, hence why earlier forms require you to give the instructions after casting. I don't see where it changes that in the reach description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:17:19-08:00","id":1039697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039502#post1039502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about this is, it's not how the spell works. It's a <i>Weaving</i> spell, which reshapes the connections of local space. The path between A and B may not exist for the target but that doesn't manifest as a cut; it manifests as a redirection. The path from A to B now redirects to C, causing anything that is along that pathway to redirect. That's how the spell is described as working. It doesn't even target the ostensible victim's Pattern; just a zero-dimensional section of space around the caster and the sympathy between it and another region.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you want, you could technically apply this as it would logically work and note that this would separate the very atoms themselves that make up the target and the energetic release would cause a nuclear explosion that would evaporate everything in an enormous radius, but I just don't think that's the intended use of the Space arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Axelgear. Your explanation seems the most logical and clear reading of the textbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T17:31:40-08:00","id":1039706,"title":"","content":"Ok, second question about Ban: What does adding Time to the spell look like? Is it possible to prevent time from moving forward within a space that ban has locked down, or would it look more like one of the time shielding spells? What happens when Time is the ONLY arcanum NOT blocked by ban? All the other arcana are fairly intuitive (perhaps Fate is also a little wonky), but Time isn't and I'd like to get the opinion of some other people as to what would happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:31:59-08:00","id":1039788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039507#post1039507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you could argue that trapping half of someone's body in a pocket dimension is the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic runs on symbolism and Space magic in particular runs on the symbolism of discrete locations being ultimately linked \u2014 as should be evident from 2e's Scale chart not being described in radii measured in imperial/metric/scientific units, a location is a discrete phenomenon as much as a person is as far as Supernal symbolism cares.<br /> <br /> The Portal Cut trick doesn't work for magic that operates through thresholds or whole-Pattern transformation of your spatial coordinates unless you're expressly using the symbolism of direct harm through spatial distortion \u2014 you might as well try to argue that deactivating a Reaching Iris early can leave someone with spirit-ephemeral hands, or that shutting a door in somebody's face does more than forcefully rebuff them before it keeps them in or out.<br /> <br /> Adding Irises to spells is almost always a Reach effect because it encourages stable instances of such to exist or be created in places like Demesnes, not because every door is a mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:45:07-08:00","id":1039831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039679#post1039679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree as the action being part of the casting. You are casting a spell to dominate their mind to allow you to send instructions, hence why earlier forms require you to give the instructions after casting. I don't see where it changes that in the reach description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Delivery of instruction is the result of casting the spell and happens in the same turn. I'm sorry but you've been interpreting this spell wrong the entire thread, I don't know how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:54:53-08:00","id":1039836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039831#post1039831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Delivery of instruction is the result of casting the spell and happens in the same turn. I'm sorry but you've been interpreting this spell wrong the entire thread, I don't know how.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fully agree I was wrong about the one word commands earlier. I went back and checked it out, but I definitely do not see in what way this part is misinterpreted. It is clear the commands come after the spell is cast, not before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:37:37-08:00","id":1039869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039836#post1039836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I fully agree I was wrong about the one word commands earlier. I went back and checked it out, but I definitely do not see in what way this part is misinterpreted. It is clear the commands come after the spell is cast, not before.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, it does not come AFTER, it goes DURING the casting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12871-elggur","name":"Elggur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:46:10-08:00","id":1039872,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> That's all very true. As mentioned to Axelgear earlier, I understand and agree that it's more in theme to have ban shunt someone sideways. I was just discussing what's been done at my table. The statement that trapping half of someone in a pocket dimension creates a situation in which they're likely to die was a non-serious attempt at picking at semantics.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8177\" data-vbnamecard=\"8177\">Heroofthemists</a> I apologize for that, but I find it hard to avoid when someone comes into a thread wielding ignorance as if it were absolute fact.<br /> <br /> During the process of defending your extremely false assertion that <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No three dots spells easily kill people. Two dots even more so </div> </div> </div> you revealed your ignorance of what level of threat Paradox actually was, how Rotes work, how Reach effects work, the actual difficulty of obtaining correct spell factors for a given effect, and how published spells work. When each of these were pointed out to you, you continually shifted goalposts, redefining what made this <i>one</i> example spell 'not easy' so you wouldn't have to face being wrong. More broadly, the assertion itself reveals a broad lack of system understanding, much less system mastery.<br /> <br /> Your unwillingness to back down on your claims even after faced with a written spell that is explicitly designed to be able to easily kill someone at two dots was incredibly frustrating, and colored my responses to you accordingly. If you'd like to further address this, please PM me, as we've derailed this thread enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-29-2017, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T00:50:07-08:00","id":1039873,"title":"","content":"New question: What Practice would you place slicing someone in half via Space at?<br /> Not a direct damage spell - one that functions as a Portal Slice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elggur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039869#post1039869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually, it does not come AFTER, it goes DURING the casting</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to come down to table preference, the spell isn't clear either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039706#post1039706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, second question about Ban: What does adding Time to the spell look like? Is it possible to prevent time from moving forward within a space that ban has locked down, or would it look more like one of the time shielding spells? What happens when Time is the ONLY arcanum NOT blocked by ban? All the other arcana are fairly intuitive (perhaps Fate is also a little wonky), but Time isn't and I'd like to get the opinion of some other people as to what would happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Time ban would look kind of like a reverse Temporal Pocket - nothing inside the ban can progress at all, while the rest of the world functions normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-29-2017, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T02:15:06-08:00","id":1039891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039873#post1039873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question: What Practice would you place slicing someone in half via Space at?<br /> Not a direct damage spell - one that functions as a Portal Slice.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is going to come down to table preference, the spell isn't clear either way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think a Time ban would look kind of like a reverse Temporal Pocket - nothing inside the ban can progress at all, while the rest of the world functions normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, like a veil of moments spell on an area? I suppose that would give a way for a Mastigos to cast the spell without requiring mana to be spent...but it does seem a little lackluster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T02:17:38-08:00","id":1039893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039891#post1039891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, like a veil of moments spell on an area? I suppose that would give a way for a Mastigos to cast the spell without requiring mana to be spent...but it does seem a little lackluster.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think the subjects in the area would be completely frozen. Kind of like the outside world is frozen when you're in a Temporal Pocket, but in reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T02:31:18-08:00","id":1039901,"title":"","content":"Oh, wow. So, what was previously a master lvl Time effect in 1e? That's...kinda what I was hoping for, but I think I'd like to hear someone else's take on it too since that is so strong.<br /> <br /> Edit: But then again, that begs the question: Since EVERYTHING is prevented from getting in or out with ban, would this also happen in a normal ban, one that did not include any other arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 01-29-2017, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T04:35:00-08:00","id":1039925,"title":"","content":"Then again, the banned area <i>does</i> already contain Time...so I'm not sure if my initial thought was correct on this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T07:36:17-08:00","id":1039978,"title":"","content":"Ban pretty much contains everything. Even attempting to step into another world causes a clash of wills. I have always been hazy on what exactly adding an arcanum to Ban changes exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","user":"Heroofthemists","date":". 01-29-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:22:16-08:00","id":1040031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039706#post1039706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, second question about Ban: What does adding Time to the spell look like? Is it possible to prevent time from moving forward within a space that ban has locked down, or would it look more like one of the time shielding spells? What happens when Time is the ONLY arcanum NOT blocked by ban? All the other arcana are fairly intuitive (perhaps Fate is also a little wonky), but Time isn't and I'd like to get the opinion of some other people as to what would happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a different reading than you've been getting. Ban doesn't cease Time from existing within the Ban. It stops Time from moving through the Ban. The effect of allowing it would be to allow someone to cast a time spell that enters the Ban without a Clash of Wills. If you disallowed Time specifically, the Time inside the Ban would continue to progress, and the Time outside the Ban would continue to progress, but they would be separate.<br /> <br /> Ban isn't Pocket Dimension that creates a new space whole cloth that wouldn't have Time, and it isn't an Unmaking spell that would destroy the Time inside of the Ban.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for adding arcana to ban, it basically allows you to create prison or shielding areas against certain arcana. A regular Ban can do this, but you'd end up suffocating someone you may want to imprison or suffocating yourself if you want to use it as a shield. That makes Forces a good addition. You may want to set up an area that allows Forces (light), Matter (air), and Mind through so you have a shielded area that requires supernatural means to enter, but that you can see out of and cast Mind spells out of at your leisure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","user":"Ifisa","date":".  Fixed the Arcana for the ban. 01-29-2017, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:23:04-08:00","id":1040033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040031#post1040031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a different reading than you've been getting. Ban doesn't cease Time from existing within the Ban. It stops Time from moving through the Ban. The effect of allowing it would be to allow someone to cast a time spell that enters the Ban without a Clash of Wills. If you disallowed Time specifically, the Time inside the Ban would continue to progress, and the Time outside the Ban would continue to progress, but they would be separate.<br /> <br /> Ban isn't Pocket Dimension that creates a new space whole cloth that wouldn't have Time, and it isn't an Unmaking spell that would destroy the Time inside of the Ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is more correct than my initial read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:31:05-08:00","id":1040042,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11862\" data-vbnamecard=\"11862\">Ifisa</a> - That actually raises some serious questions about the setting: Does Time flow <i>from</i> somewhere and, hence, through the Fallen World, or is it a quantity something has? If a Ban focused on Time causes things inside the Ban to stop aging, it has a fairly profound metaphysical implication regarding the structure of the universe, as does the alternative.<br /> <br /> As it stands, though, I agree with you; the intended purpose of the Ban would be to prevent Time spells or effects from crossing into or out of the Ban area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 01-29-2017, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:33:25-08:00","id":1040045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040031#post1040031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may want to set up an area that allows Forces (light and air)</div> </div> </div> </div>Air isn't under the purview of Forces, that's Matter. Everything else is right though.<br /> <br /> Actually, your mention of Time inside and outside of the Ban progressing separately is kind of intriguing. I'm not sure what kind of shenanigans that would enable, but I know I want to find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:56:12-08:00","id":1040060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040045#post1040045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Air isn't under the purview of Forces, that's Matter. Everything else is right though.<br /> <br /> Actually, your mention of Time inside and outside of the Ban progressing separately is kind of intriguing. I'm not sure what kind of shenanigans that would enable, but I know I want to find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right about that, I was working off an erroneous memory of the Pocket Dimension spell that specifically says Matter and I thought said Forces. As for operating separately, I think it would only really affect Supernal spells. Someone drops a giant scale spell to revert everything in a parking lot to its state 20 years ago, but once its cast you are standing in your matter/forces exempt Ban and you appear to be standing in a circle of pavement in a field full of babies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:07:28-08:00","id":1040072,"title":"","content":"I imagine if you used a Time-Ban an a portion of a vessel traveling at relativistic speeds, time inside the ban would flow at the same rate it would have from its original point of reference. That's the only strange interaction I can think of that doesn't <i>just</i> involve blocking out Time magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:42:06-08:00","id":1040251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040042#post1040042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11862\" data-vbnamecard=\"11862\">Ifisa</a> - That actually raises some serious questions about the setting: Does Time flow <i>from</i> somewhere and, hence, through the Fallen World, or is it a quantity something has?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quarantine suggests the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T00:45:18-08:00","id":1040482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1039873#post1039873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question: What Practice would you place slicing someone in half via Space at?<br /> Not a direct damage spell - one that functions as a Portal Slice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say unmaking myself. Per the Sympathy rules, it's level 5 that you gain the ability to effect the connections of something that is metaphysically the same object. Since your top half and bottom half are the same 'object' according to space, disconnecting them with space would be unmaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 01-30-2017, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:03:01-08:00","id":1040516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Splinter (Space </span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Unraveling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand: </span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills:</span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medicine, Firearms, Brawl</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All things are dependent on the Supernal for their reality. By unraveling the threads of a subject's Tapestry, the Mage denies their opponent the very existence of their parts.With this spell, the Mage may inflict one Tilt affecting the target's limbs (Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Blinded, Deafened) per dot of Potency. Applying the tilt twice affects both bodily members. This may manifest as nerve damage, sapping of strength, or even the limbs simply turning cold and dead.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The spell is not clean and gentle; the unraveled threads explode outwards and turn the subject's limbs into a shower of gore. For each Tilt inflicted, the subject suffers one lethal health level. The damage does not disappear when the Tilts end.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+2 Reach and 1 Mana:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rather than merely sapping the strength from the target's limbs, the Mage severs them entirely. This renders the effect Lasting.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that it's an Unraveling effect, not Unmaking which could get rid of whole buildings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:54:32-08:00","id":1040769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040516#post1040516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that it's an Unraveling effect, not Unmaking which could get rid of whole buildings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that is brutal. I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:41:54-08:00","id":1040907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040516#post1040516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that it's an Unraveling effect, not Unmaking which could get rid of whole buildings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, given the description of the different practices, I'd have to agree with you there. Unmaking would simply completely destroy the body, not simply sever a limb (heads count! at least grammatically, though probably not supernally).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:46:59-08:00","id":1040912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040516#post1040516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that it's an Unraveling effect, not Unmaking which could get rid of whole buildings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the reality of things is that no matter what level of an Arcana, you can effect a person or whole buildings. A practice does not decide 'you can now do this to a building'. If you are creating an effect that can slice something in half, it's not an effect that is limited to only one person - it's an effect that you can use against swarms of people, and if you can cut a person in half there is no reason you should not be able to cut a building in half - besides a difference in scale. I can teleport a whole building the same way I could teleport a person (though one would, of course, be much more noticeable)<br /> <br /> In the Space Arcana, the mechanics of space are governed by sympathy. What you can effect is based on the connection between two things. The reason I would think it unmaking is that, in order to dissolve the bond of space between two things that are connected (according to space - the same thing), you need an Unmaking Effect (Sympathy Chart, MtA pg 172).<br /> <br /> With this custom spell here, you make the ability to tear a person's limb off permanently. If I could remove permanently their arm, why exactly could I not do that with their head, and automatically kill them? Why, metaphysically, would a head, torso, or heart be connected to the body differently from a hand or foot? Keep in mind - space is not affecting the limbs themselves - it's effecting the space which the limbs make up. Severing a limb (or more) is disconnecting the space between one part of a body with the space of another part.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:52:54-08:00","id":1040918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040912#post1040912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the reality of things is that no matter what level of an Arcana, you can effect a person or whole buildings. A practice does not decide 'you can now do this to a building'. If you are creating an effect that can slice something in half, it's not an effect that is limited to only one person - it's an effect that you can use against swarms of people, and if you can cut a person in half there is no reason you should not be able to cut a building in half - besides a difference in scale. I can teleport a whole building the same way I could teleport a person (though one would, of course, be much more noticeable)<br /> <br /> In the Space Arcana, the mechanics of space are governed by sympathy. What you can effect is based on the connection between two things. The reason I would think it unmaking is that, in order to dissolve the bond of space between two things that are connected (according to space - the same thing), you need an Unmaking Effect (Sympathy Chart, MtA pg 172).<br /> <br /> With this custom spell here, you make the ability to tear a person's limb off permanently. If I could remove permanently their arm, why exactly could I not do that with their head, and automatically kill them? Why, metaphysically, would a head, torso, or heart be connected to the body differently from a hand or foot? Keep in mind - space is not affecting the limbs themselves - it's effecting the space which the limbs make up. Severing a limb (or more) is disconnecting the space between one part of a body with the space of another part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with your analysis is in the description of the practices themselves:<br /> <br /> Unraveling spells can significantly impair or damage phe-<br /> nomena under the Arcanum\u2019s purview, or directly inflict severe<br /> damage using the forces of an Arcanum. A raging storm might<br /> become a calm summer\u2019s day (Forces), or solid iron reduced to<br /> dust (Matter); even spells can be torn asunder (Prime). Mages<br /> can hurl fire (Forces) at their enemies, or cause aneurysms and<br /> heart attacks with a glance (Mind or Life). Damage inflicted<br /> by a direct Unraveling attack is lethal, but can be upgraded to<br /> aggravated by spending a point of Mana and one Reach.<br /> <br /> Unmaking spells annihilate subjects under the Arcanum\u2019s<br /> purview entirely. Life can be snuffed like a candle (Life),<br /> two locations can be forced into each other by destroying<br /> the distance between them (Space), even Hallows and<br /> Verges can be wiped from the Earth (Prime). Unmaking<br /> spells are beyond inflicting direct damage with attacks; A<br /> SUCCESSFUL UNMAKING DESTROYS THE TARGET ALTOGETHER.<br /> <br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Severing a limb might (and very likely would) kill a person, but it doesn't destroy the person altogether. The fact that you are manipulating the space that a person occupies is irrelavent; the PERSON is still the target of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:00:01-08:00","id":1040923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040912#post1040912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With this custom spell here, you make the ability to tear a person's limb off permanently. If I could remove permanently their arm, <b>why exactly could I not do that with their head, and automatically kill them?</b> Why, metaphysically, would a head, torso, or heart be connected to the body differently from a hand or foot? </div> </div> </div> </div>Why couldn't you? The answer is simple really. You could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:02:12-08:00","id":1040926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040918#post1040918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with your analysis is in the description of the practices themselves:<br /> <br /> Unraveling spells can significantly impair or damage phe-<br /> nomena under the Arcanum\u2019s purview, or directly inflict severe<br /> damage using the forces of an Arcanum. A raging storm might<br /> become a calm summer\u2019s day (Forces), or solid iron reduced to<br /> dust (Matter); even spells can be torn asunder (Prime). Mages<br /> can hurl fire (Forces) at their enemies, or cause aneurysms and<br /> heart attacks with a glance (Mind or Life). Damage inflicted<br /> by a direct Unraveling attack is lethal, but can be upgraded to<br /> aggravated by spending a point of Mana and one Reach.<br /> <br /> Unmaking spells annihilate subjects under the Arcanum\u2019s<br /> purview entirely. Life can be snuffed like a candle (Life),<br /> two locations can be forced into each other by destroying<br /> the distance between them (Space), even Hallows and<br /> Verges can be wiped from the Earth (Prime). Unmaking<br /> spells are beyond inflicting direct damage with attacks; A<br /> SUCCESSFUL UNMAKING DESTROYS THE TARGET ALTOGETHER.<br /> <br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Severing a limb might (and very likely would) kill a person, but it doesn't destroy the person altogether. The fact that you are manipulating the space that a person occupies is irrelavent; the PERSON is still the target of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Unmaking the connection between a person's head and a person's neck is exactly that - destroying that connection. Your not affecting the person themselves - your affecting the connections that make up the person, the space surrounding them. If your not unmaking that connection, then the neck, arms, feet - they are still connected and the same subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sympathy Chart, pg 172</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Connected: The two subjects are metaphysically one e.g. a mage and her familiar or soul stone. The connection is unassailable without Unmaking magic and casting using the connection is not Withstood.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I'm observing here, is that the connection between a person's hand and their arm is of a Connected Sympathy. They are metaphysically (and physically!) connected - and effecting that connection is blatantly stated as requiring unmaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:06:02-08:00","id":1040929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040923#post1040923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why couldn't you? The answer is simple really. You could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so your thoughts on this spell are, with 2 reach and a mana, you'd no longer be be limited to dealing damage but automatically killing your target? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That does seem more in line with unmaking at that point, on a mechanics level as well as a metaphysics level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:44:07-08:00","id":1040949,"title":"","content":"Killing a target has nothing to do with a Practice. Veiling can kill people too - just Veil air as a balcony. I hope that I don't need to mention Psychic Domination and Ban. It's not a game about killing but about choices. You don't really struggle to kill. <br /> And there is a difference between Unmaking and causing a crack. With Unmaking you can dissapear your target, With Unraveling you can dismember it. If you feel like killing someone is always a fifth dot effect just put it there. Just remember that creating persistant conditions is a four dot effect and severed arm is exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:48:41-08:00","id":1040952,"title":"","content":"Since we're on the subject of Bans. Could you use a ban to prevent being grappled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:51:34-08:00","id":1040954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040926#post1040926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. Unmaking the connection between a person's head and a person's neck is exactly that - destroying that connection. Your not affecting the person themselves - your affecting the connections that make up the person, the space surrounding them. If your not unmaking that connection, then the neck, arms, feet - they are still connected and the same subject.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All I'm observing here, is that the connection between a person's hand and their arm is of a Connected Sympathy. They are metaphysically (and physically!) connected - and effecting that connection is blatantly stated as requiring unmaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, the target is the person, NOT their sympathetic connection to themselves. You're manipulating the false distance between one piece of tissue and another, not the real closeness of their sympathetic connection to themselves. <br /> <br /> On top of that, what do you think it looks like when aggravated damage is done to a person? Severing a limb is VERY appropriate for such a thing, and unraveling is capable of causing aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:55:13-08:00","id":1040956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040952#post1040952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're on the subject of Bans. Could you use a ban to prevent being grappled?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're inside it, or the person wanting to grapple you is, and only you have Space or some other power that would allow you to breach the Ban then yes. Isn't that obvious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:59:50-08:00","id":1040958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040956#post1040956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're inside it, or the person wanting to grapple you is, and only you have Space or some other power that would allow you to breach the Ban then yes. Isn't that obvious?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is but I'm still fairly new to the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T16:23:06-08:00","id":1040968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040949#post1040949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing a target has nothing to do with a Practice. Veiling can kill people too - just Veil air as a balcony. I hope that I don't need to mention Psychic Domination and Ban. It's not a game about killing but about choices. You don't really struggle to kill.<br /> And there is a difference between Unmaking and causing a crack. With Unmaking you can dissapear your target, With Unraveling you can dismember it. If you feel like killing someone is always a fifth dot effect just put it there. Just remember that creating persistant conditions is a four dot effect and severed arm is exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is... true enough, even if I'm not entirely sure I understand what you mean by &quot;veil air as a balcony&quot;. I do know you can create circumstances that cause damage to a person - and that you can create a circumstance that will end in the death of a person without much they can do about it. It's when that automatically kills something, without damage actually needing to be involved (which damage is with P.D. and Ban-Style Suffocation) that, mechanically speaking, it should fall into the realm of unmaking. If you cast it, and they die automatically, unmaking, If you cast it and they suffer damage = potency or x damage over time or they blow their brains out with a killing blow - totally any number of other practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040954#post1040954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once again, the target is the person, NOT their sympathetic connection to themselves. You're manipulating the false distance between one piece of tissue and another, not the real closeness of their sympathetic connection to themselves.<br /> <br /> On top of that, what do you think it looks like when aggravated damage is done to a person? Severing a limb is VERY appropriate for such a thing, and unraveling is capable of causing aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure - I can see severing a limb as an aggravated damage effect. That's not what I'm arguing at all - I'm arguing the fact that that's not quite how one would use space to that effect. There is a reason instead of ripping a person's limbs off they had people clashing into objects and existing in the same space - that was how they utilized their 'damage' effects. Similarly, warp can cripple an arm or leg by warping the space that a person is in and causing their body to tear due to the positions that they are placed in - but it doesn't actually disconnect the person from themselves. At the end of the day, space still decides that that arm is, in fact, a part of them. I could even see a version of warp dealing lethal and agg that savagely shifts their arm around their other arm causing a third degree break with bones ripping out of flesh and gushing blood. I could even see you warping a piece of metal into a person's arm and causing -that- to slice the arm or limb off. It's actually disconnecting one part of the body from the other via space and space alone that is what I'm saying is unmaking.<br /> <br /> My arguement is exactly that: The target is the person - they are themselves. Disconnecting them from themselves is impossible without unmaking, because they are still, in fact, one single person. If they had, for instance, a prosthetic arm instead of a physical one, disconnecting that from them might be different - it's not a part of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T05:09:49-08:00","id":1041204,"title":"","content":"Have you ever torn a piece of cloth before? It's not easy to get exactly the part you want, but if you unravel the threads holding that piece together it is easier. Naturally it's easier to simply cut the cloth, but if scissors or a knife isn't available, you may have to use a combination of brute strength, ingenuity, and patience. <br /> <br /> Similarly, I find it patently absurd that someone couldn't sever a limb with unraveling of Space. It won't be easy or clean (reaching), but it can be done. Just because Collapse is the spell the book uses doesn't mean that that attack spell is the be all end all for Space unraveling attack spells. There's this thing called creative thaumaturgy that lets us make new spells. Ergo, severed limbs via Space unraveling.<br /> <br /> That being said, I personally find the challenge of not killing your opponent to be more thrilling. Can you truly dominate them such that you don't even have to think of using violence, let alone actually commit it? If you ask me, THAT'S a big part of being one of the Wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T06:22:12-08:00","id":1041223,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a> You have now misinterpreted the point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> is making several times. You'd probably do better in this conversation if you read their post more closely so you could accurately respond to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:00:05-08:00","id":1041233,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> Are you saying that you need to be a master to cut a tree for a fireplace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:36:55-08:00","id":1041247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040968#post1040968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My arguement is exactly that: The target is the person - they are themselves. Disconnecting them from themselves is impossible without unmaking, because they are still, in fact, one single person. If they had, for instance, a prosthetic arm instead of a physical one, disconnecting that from them might be different - it's not a part of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I am understanding from this is:<br /> <br /> To cause the sympathy of something with itself (not just something an intimate connection, but actually part of the same thing) to be severed so severely that it isn't even part of the same thing anymore is to <i>unmake that sympathy in a fell swoop</i>, thus the unmake practice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041204#post1041204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever torn a piece of cloth before? It's not easy to get exactly the part you want, but if you unravel the threads holding that piece together it is easier. Naturally it's easier to simply cut the cloth, but if scissors or a knife isn't available, you may have to use a combination of brute strength, ingenuity, and patience.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I find it patently absurd that someone couldn't sever a limb with unraveling of Space. It won't be easy or clean (reaching), but it can be done. Just because Collapse is the spell the book uses doesn't mean that that attack spell is the be all end all for Space unraveling attack spells. -snip- <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><i>see below</i></span> -snip- Ergo, severed limbs via Space unraveling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your tearing analogy seems very much like this description:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1040968#post1040968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, warp can cripple an arm or leg by warping the space that a person is in and causing their body to tear due to the positions that they are placed in - but it doesn't actually disconnect the person from themselves. At the end of the day, space still decides that that arm is, in fact, a part of them. I could even see a version of warp dealing lethal and agg that savagely shifts their arm around their other arm causing a third degree break with bones ripping out of flesh and gushing blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041204#post1041204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's this thing called creative thaumaturgy that lets us make new spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what you are describing is not a spell in and of itself, nor should it be based on what is governed by the practices, but rather repeated applications of the spell <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> is describing above. (Obviously repeated Unraveling can eventually functionally &quot;Unmake&quot; something). Fraying, Unraveling, and Unmaking are all the same thing after all and are only different in the degree at which they function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:10:02-08:00","id":1041264,"title":"","content":"You don't need to Unmake anything, you just need to pull from two sides really hard. It's far from Unmaking.<br /> And about Unraveling that you say can't change subject so much that it isn't itself anymore... Well. Unraveling/Patterning does exactly that.<br /> <br /> Edit: How can you accept twisting and bruising your target by manipulating space around them but not acknowledging the immense force that comes from moving space itself around? Your target is not really your target in this case. Its a place where he stands and damage done to him is just a byproduct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-31-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:19:15-08:00","id":1041272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041264#post1041264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to Unmake anything, you just need to pull from two sides really hard. It's far from Unmaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;pull from two sides really hard&quot; implies imparting kinetic force with is governed by Forces. Remember Space moves things with adding or removing force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041264#post1041264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And about Unraveling that you say can't change subject so much that it isn't itself anymore... Well. Unraveling/Patterning does exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>To which I say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041247#post1041247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what you are describing is not a spell in and of itself, nor should it be based on what is governed by the practices, but rather repeated applications of the spell <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> is describing above. (Obviously repeated Unraveling can eventually functionally &quot;Unmake&quot; something). <u>Fraying, Unraveling, and Unmaking are all the same thing after all <i>and are only different in the degree at which they function</i></u><i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Underlined and italics for emphasis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:30:28-08:00","id":1041280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041272#post1041272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;pull from two sides really hard&quot; implies kenetic force with is governed by Forces. Remember Space moves things with adding or removing force.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll repeat my edit from above, sorry for that mess:<br /> <br /> How can you accept twisting and bruising your target by manipulating space around them but not acknowledging the immense force that comes from moving space itself around? Your target is not really your target in this case. Its a place where he stands and damage done to him is just a byproduct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:48:07-08:00","id":1041291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041280#post1041280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll repeat my edit from above, sorry for that mess:<br /> <br /> How can you accept twisting and bruising your target by manipulating space around them but not acknowledging the immense force that comes from moving space itself around? Your target is not really your target in this case. Its a place where he stands and damage done to him is just a byproduct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unraveling is shown to cause damage when causing things to occupy the same Space. I mean that is the whole point of the Collapse spell (MtA 2nd Pg. 177). Could those &quot;things&quot; be different parts of the same thing? I say absolutely (at my table I'd assign Reach because that's a bit of a complex visualization). Would that functionally look like using the damage from the Collapse spell to cause enough tissue damage to sever the arm? I would think so. Is it force, I picture it as using Space to tightly fold sections of the arm over and over again until the crease (damage in this case) causes the severing.<br /> <br /> This is why I say that arm severing with unraveling would not be a spell in and of itself, but rather a radical degree of success of an existing spell. To just cleanly remove the thing with a single success on the spell, that'd be unmaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:08:58-08:00","id":1041302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041291#post1041291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unraveling is shown to cause damage when causing things to occupy the same Space. I mean that is the whole point of the Collapse spell (MtA 2nd Pg. 177). Could those &quot;things&quot; be different parts of the same thing? I say absolutely (at my table I'd assign Reach because that's a bit of a complex visualization). Would that functionally look like using the damage from the Collapse spell to cause enough tissue damage to sever the arm? I would think so. Is it force, I picture it as using Space to tightly fold sections of the arm over and over again until the crease (damage in this case) causes the severing.<br /> <br /> This is why I say that arm severing with unraveling would not be a spell in and of itself, but rather a radical degree of success of an existing spell. To just cleanly remove the thing with a single success on the spell, that'd be unmaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potency and Reach options <i>are </i>a degree of success, not a roll that says you made it or not. If you don't see it that way I guess you can limit this Reach effect to spells that deal aggraveted damage in excess to stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:31:20-08:00","id":1041335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041302#post1041302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Potency and Reach options <i>are </i>a degree of success, not a roll that says you made it or not. If you don't see it that way I guess you can limit this Reach effect to spells that deal aggraveted damage in excess to stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Potency is the degree which determines damage. Reach determines if it is Aggravated. See this -&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/800994-cofd-massive-damage-destroying-limbs-and-organs?p=801186#post801186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's written on the Tilts themselves, under &quot;Causing the Tilt&quot;. In the case of Arm Wrack and Leg Wrack, they're caused by targeted attacks to the arms or legs that deal more damage than the target's stamina. If the damage was aggravated, the limb is cut off, destroyed, or otherwise made permanently useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between Unraveling to sever an arm with Space and using Unmake with Space, is that in Unravel you're using the spell as a way to meet the mundane requirements to sever a limb (a set amount of aggravated Damage to a limb) and with Unmaking you can much more cleanly (ie without meeting the needed amount of Aggravated damage requirement) to apply a Lasting Arm Wrack Tilt without applying any damage at all. -pop- The limb drops off painlessly. In a way, the Unmaking method is a lot more horrifying (though possibly less terrifying) than the more gruesome Unraveling method.<br /> <br /> This whole discussion makes me think of Life \u2022 Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Rotes that use a variant of Quarantine to temporarily lobotomize, castrate, or otherwise remove a part that may or may not cause death due to their absence from people. (Quarantine because it pops back after spell duration).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:48:47-08:00","id":1041341,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> What Charlaquin said is a short version of rules for applying Tilts <i>without </i>magic. Don't confuse those mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creating a Persistent Condition is almost always a Patterning<br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Unraveling (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) effect. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tilts are usually created by applying a Reach to an attack<br /> spell, <b>but if you want to create one on its own, it\u2019s usually<br /> a Fraying (\u2022\u2022\u2022) or Patterning (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) spell.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:01:46-08:00","id":1041349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041341#post1041341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> What Charlaquin said is a short version of rules for applying Tilts <i>without </i>magic. Don't confuse those mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also on page 126 of Mage: The Awakening 2nd Ed (right above the guidelines you posted)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA pg 126</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the effects of Conditions and Tilts are so broad, it\u2019s difficult to assign hard-and-fast rules for Practices that inflict them. Use the Practice descriptions and the following list as a guideline:</div> </div> </div> </div>Self admitting not hard and fast rules, but rather guidelines. So I have a couple questions, is one of your arguments that Unmaking is the wrong practice to simply remove/obliterate the connection between two points of the same object or being? Also are you arguing an Unravel Space spell shouldn't need more than one success to pop off an arm with a persistent Arm Wracked Condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:27:14-08:00","id":1041359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041349#post1041349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also are you arguing an Unravel Space spell shouldn't need more than one success to pop off an arm with a persistent Arm Wracked Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of the outcome of this discussion, spells don't require more than one success to achieve their result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:29:26-08:00","id":1041360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041349#post1041349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Self admitting not hard and fast rules, but rather guidelines. So I have a couple questions, is one of your arguments that Unmaking is the wrong practice to simply remove/obliterate the connection between two points of the same object or being? Also are you arguing an Unravel Space spell shouldn't need more than one success to pop off an arm with a persistent Arm Wracked Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unmaking is a great practice to do this, a little show of though. There are many ways to achieve an effect: you can Fray someones energy to make him tired that he falls asleep an the spot or simply command him to sleep with Rulling.<br /> <br /> No spell should need more than one success to achieve it's results. All you need to account are Withstand and Reach options - which this spell operates on.<br /> <br /> They may be just guidelines but they are in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:42:55-08:00","id":1041369,"title":"","content":"I'm coming in late, but the discussion about the Sympathetic Connection chart isn't applicable to discussing a spell that would sever your limb from your body. The discussion about Unmaking in the chart applies to the Sympathetic Connection only, for instance if you wanted to sever a person's Sympathetic Connection to their own arm for some reason (maybe it would make it impossible to use Mudra that rely on hand gestures?). If you want to sever the arm itself, the withstand would be based on their pattern, likely Stamina, because you aren't adjusting the Sympathy between a person and their limb. The Connected Sympathy would immediately begin to degrade once the limb is severed due to the naturally occurring phenomena around Sympathy, similar to how the Sympathetic Connection for bodily samples is only Strong. That's a side effect, though, not a direct assault.<br /> <br /> Example: Unmaking a Mage's Familiar, that is Sympathetically Connected to them, should only take Spirit 5. Despite the Sympathetic Connection, it wouldn't require Space 5. I think the issue here is mainly arising due to the Space Arcanum covering both Sympathetic Connections and Distances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","user":"Ifisa","date":". 01-31-2017, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:03:12-08:00","id":1041384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041369#post1041369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Example: Unmaking a Mage's Familiar, that is Sympathetically Connected to them, should only take Spirit 5. Despite the Sympathetic Connection, it wouldn't require Space 5. I think the issue here is mainly arising due to the Space Arcanum covering both Sympathetic Connections and Distances.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not unmaking the sympathetic connection though, it's unmaking the thing that the sympathetic connection happens to be a byproduct of. Same with how matter unmaking on your wedding ring isn't unmaking the sympathetic connection, it's unmaking the thing the sympathetic connection is tied to and getting rid of the sympathy as a byproduct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:04:43-08:00","id":1041385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041384#post1041384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not unmaking the sympathetic connection though, it's unmaking the thing that the sympathetic connection happens to be a byproduct of. Same with how matter unmaking on your wedding ring isn't unmaking the sympathetic connection, it's unmaking the thing the sympathetic connection is tied to and getting rid of the sympathy as a byproduct.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point, cutting off the arm by unraveling the space enough (Aggravated damage) is definitely possible and doesn't have anything to do with the Sympathetic Withstand chart referencing the need for Unmaking spells to affect Connected Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:06:07-08:00","id":1041387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041360#post1041360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No spell should need more than one success to achieve it's results. All you need to account are Withstand and Reach options - which this spell operates on.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041359#post1041359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of the outcome of this discussion, spells don't require more than one success to achieve their result.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you both are saying. What you are saying is correct in a particular context but misses the following nuance: You can't inflict 5 points of damage with a spell that inflicts a 1 point of damage per Potency with a single success. That is precisely the type of degrees of success I am talking about, and was quite explicit in explaining <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041335#post1041335\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I am not disputing whether Space can sever an arm, or arguing that it's impossible to sever an arm with Unravel using Space. I am saying that is the level of Space Arcanum mastery where it first introduces the ability to inflict damage at all, and it'd be entirely appropriate to treat the magical attack using that Arcanum at that level of mastery as just another source of damage for purposes of cutting off arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:26:12-08:00","id":1041399,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> You do know that you need more than one Potency (as you call it - successess) to affect Withstood target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:02:14-08:00","id":1041425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041399#post1041399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> You do know that you need more than one Potency (as you call it - successess) to affect Withstood target?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do know that, but I also know:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA 2nd Ed pg 127</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells that inflict direct damage with the Practices of Fraying and Unraveling are never Withstood; the subject\u2019s Stamina is already factored in by virtue of the subject\u2019s Health.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that brings up a good point that the Space Unmaking arm-popping-off spell would naturally be Withstood with Stamina.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA 2nd Ed pg 127</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain Unmaking (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) spells can slay a target with a single casting, or neutralize them permanently, but even then, the spell is always Withstood by the target\u2019s relevant Resistance Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for bringing that up, I had forgot that. So either way, no one Potency arm-popping-off spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:13:17-08:00","id":1041434,"title":"","content":"Not going to weigh in on the Unraveling/Unmaking debate, but:<br /> <br /> An arm sundering spell isn't (necessarily) going to be a direct damage spell. Attempts to shoehorn it into that role make Creative Thaumauturgists cry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:49:40-08:00","id":1041453,"title":"","content":"Is this whole conversation so some Mastigos player can make a gauche pun about &quot;disarming&quot; someone?<br /> <br /> if so +1 internet for baiting me into taking it seriously. If not, +2 internets for making Creative Thaumauturgists cry as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> said. (I also agree that an arm sundering spell doesn't have to cause damage, I was just arguing at what mastery of Space Arcanum that'd be.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:43:14-08:00","id":1041488,"title":"","content":"At times like this I wish I had this 'summon Dave' magical button, because we are not going anywhere with this problem.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041425#post1041425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for bringing that up, I had forgot that. So either way, no one Potency arm-popping-off spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you check again the spell that I presented you'll find that its Withstood just fine. But its not neutralizing permanently a target.<br /> <br /> Edit: I would allow it to slay a target with proper Reach, though. Space Arcanum has nothing to do with symbols of death or life. It doesn't care. All that matters is space that someone happens to occupy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-31-2017, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:20:04-08:00","id":1041512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041488#post1041488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At times like this I wish I had this 'summon Dave' magical button, because we are not going anywhere with this problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a neat artifact. I don't view this so much as a problem, but rather as an enjoyable debate. While I'd like to be right (and ultimately will be even if I am not current, since I am willing to change my point of view if given evidence to do so), I am also just having fun chatting about arcane minutiae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041488#post1041488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I would allow it to slay a target with proper Reach, though. Space Arcanum has nothing to do with symbols of death or life. It doesn't care. All that matters is space that someone happens to occupy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the Arcanum cares neither for life nor death. It seemed you were referencing Space as a location within the three axis of absolute dimensional measurement, rather than a gross relative confluence of connections between <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/thing\" target=\"_blank\">things</a>, in that last sentence. Is that your stance for the Arcanum? My interpretation is the latter. By the way, I am really enjoying your ability to articulate your point of view and reference material to back up your assertions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:47:46-08:00","id":1041530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041387#post1041387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't inflict 5 points of damage with a spell that inflicts a 1 point of damage per Potency with a single success.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly how spells work. You have it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:50:50-08:00","id":1041533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039383-ban?p=1041512#post1041512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be a neat artifact. I don't view this so much as a problem, but rather as an enjoyable debate. While I'd like to be right (and ultimately will be even if I am not current, since I am willing to change my point of view if given evidence to do so), I am also just having fun chatting about arcane minutiae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree that the Arcanum cares neither for life nor death. It seemed you were referencing Space as a location within the three axis of absolute dimensional measurement, rather than a gross relative confluence of connections between <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://www.dictionary.com/browse/thing&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">things</a>, in that last sentence. Is that your stance for the Arcanum? My interpretation is the latter. By the way, I am really enjoying your ability to articulate your point of view and reference material to back up your assertions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't either or, it is both. The Space arcanum treats both phenomena as seperate concepts, one being made up of the Lie, the other of Supernal truth, both falling under its purview. Space is capable of manipulating both. In this particular case, the latter has absolutely nothing to do with how one would accomplish severing a limb. It's strictly a manipulation of the former, and as such you don't need to unmake anything.<br /> <br /> As enjoyable I find considering the minutia of the arcane myself, this thread has been off its rails for a while. My questions concerning the ban spell have been answered. If you all wish to continue conversing about the other topics, you should probably start another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:48:58-08:00","id":1041568,"title":"","content":"Very well Falcon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I will go ahead and start a new thread for the purposes of this discussion. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041573-slicing-a-person-in-half-via-space\">For those interested</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 01-31-2017, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T12:00:37-08:00","id":1045894,"title":"","content":"Ban doesn't cut things in half, and it doesn't have to do with practices or balance. I know because Dave used my corrected wording for it XD<br /> <br /> If someone casts a Ban over an area and the border of the Ban is crossing through the middle of your body, then one half of your body is on one side of the banned area and the other side is now across the opposite side of the banned area, both halves remain together unharmed because there is no intervening distance between them while the ban is in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T01:36:33-08:00","id":1047124,"title":"","content":"Would this mean say i have a ban vs humans in a room on the 80th floor that extends to just outside the wall of the room. A person attempts to enter the banned room via the door and gets looped to the other side of the ban which is opposite the door and then falls to his death? I assume the person at the door would see the odd lens effect and see a door that ends at midair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T03:06:20-08:00","id":1047142,"title":"","content":"Yes. But you could Veil the distortion with another Space spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}